    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Brady House** emerging as our premier offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.57) holds the highest daily efficiency score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Meyer and a +14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Brady House** (63.18) offers significant upside against Woods Richardson; the combination of a +19% SP skill adjustment and his prime spot in the heart of the order makes him a must-start, even as we prioritize high-floor production across the board. While **Jackson Merrill** (60.00) faces a tougher test against the southpaw Liberatore, his elite leadoff placement and strong SP skill rating solidify his status as a cornerstone play for today\u2019s 5x5 categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just outside our active threshold at 37.37. While **Coby Mayo** carries legitimate power potential, he was squeezed out of the utility slot due to the superior matchup efficiency of **Brady House** and the risk-averse nature of our current scoring floor. We are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (40.61), who narrowly cleared the bench cutoff; his profile is heavily impacted by the platoon disadvantage against Povich, and any further degradation in his projected lineup spot could force a pivot. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined due to scheduling or injury, our depth is being tested, making it critical that **Nasim Nunez** (59.75) maximizes his opportunity against Woods Richardson to capitalize on his elite speed potential in a favorable park environment.",
